calls.reply:

  "name": "The Divine Right of the Tsar",
  "aka": [
    {
      "name": "Divine Right Doctrine",
      "tag": "common",
      "everyday": true
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Divine Right of the Tsar is the doctrine of the Church of the Eternal Vigil that the Tsar of Moscavia rules by divine will, having been placed upon the throne by God's direct appointment.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The doctrine holds that the Tsar is not merely a political leader but a divinely anointed sovereign whose authority flows from the same source as the Great Changing itself — the will of God as revealed through the sacred night.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Tsar is considered the earthly representative of God's covenant with Moscavia, and his rule is understood to be inseparable from the sanctity of the owl-folk transformation.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "According to the doctrine, resistance to the Tsar's authority is resistance to God, and obedience to the Tsar is a sacred duty incumbent upon all owl-folk.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Patriarch of Moscavia is charged with formally recognizing the legitimacy of each new Tsar through a consecration ceremony performed at the Temple of the First Changing in Moskov.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The doctrine asserts that the Tsar's power is not granted by the people or by tradition alone but is sustained by ongoing divine favor, which can be withdrawn if the Tsar forsakes the faith.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Tsar is expected to govern in accordance with the teachings of the Church of the Eternal Vigil, and the Ecumenical Council reserves the right to counsel the Tsar on matters of faith and morality.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Divine Right Doctrine is taught in every temple and seminary of the Vigil as foundational to Moscavian identity, woven into the Nocturnal Vigil and the Moonrise Sermon alike.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "No secular law enacted by the Tsar may contradict Church doctrine, and any such law is considered void in the eyes of the faithful.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The doctrine does not teach that the Tsar is infallible in all personal matters, only that his authority to rule is divinely ordained and must be respected by all subjects.",
